{
  "name": "How Do I Get My Porcelain Tile to Last?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Want your new porcelain tile to stand the test of time? It all starts with a solid installation and careful consideration of your tile choice. First off, make sure your substrate is impeccable – clean, level, and totally stable. Any unevenness underneath will eventually show through or cause cracks. Secondly, it’s critical to use the right adhesive and ensure full mortar coverage under each tile. Skipping this step leads to hollow spots, which can cause tiles to crack under pressure. Next, proper alignment and spacing are key for both aesthetics and durability; 'lippage' (uneven tile edges) is a no-go. Don't forget about movement joints either, especially in larger areas or over existing surfaces, as they help accommodate natural expansion and contraction. Lastly, respect those cure times! Mortar and grout need adequate time to dry and harden before you put them to the test. If you're working with large-format porcelain or a complex design, bringing in a seasoned pro is a smart move. HH Remodeling LLC has the expertise to make sure your porcelain tile isn't just beautiful, but built to last.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
